# Testing

- Run the test framework, scripts, and helpers already configured. Do not add a second test stack.
- Cover the behavior that changed, including a regression for a fixed bug and an integration check when the change crosses a boundary.
- Keep tests deterministic. Control time, network, and shared state instead of depending on them.
- Assert observable outcomes. Do not couple tests to private implementation details.
- Do not report a test as passed unless that command was run in this session and its result was seen.
